# CenturionAI Remote — locked design (v1.1)

Canonical spec: [ios/CenturionApp/DESIGN_RULES.md](ios/CenturionApp/DESIGN_RULES.md)

## Language (default UI)

Never: LLM, provider, Bonjour, mDNS, API key, model slug, file paths.
Always: your Centurion, private connection, thinking service, Get Help, your mission.

## Calm Remote UX (locked)

- **Device link** and **thinking service** are separate — never one merged status on default surfaces.
- **Get Help** requires device link (support codes, auto-fix on host).
- Max **one filled primary CTA** per screen on Connect.
- Recoverable errors: plain words + retry; never simulated success when disconnected.

## Adrian online (locked)

- Adrian is **Adrian online** — founder voice, cloud-hosted (`adrian.centurion.ai`), Centurion-paid; users never bring API keys.
- **Placement only:** Connect (`Talk to Adrian` beside Get Help) and You → Support. **No** floating/global Adrian on Chat, Home, or Privacy.
- **North star:** help users live their **evolving mission** — lift pressure, free thinking, 1:1 with private Centurion.
- **Personality:** understand first; Loop (one step at a time); expert before advising; AI speed + human creativity.
- **Privacy:** sanitized context only; never Centurion chat history or secrets.
- Keep iOS welcome (`AdrianService.seedWelcomeIfNeeded`), privacy gate (`AdrianView`), and backend (`centurion_cli/adrian/prompts.py`, `knowledge.md`) aligned.

## PR review

Any change to `ios/CenturionApp/Views/` must pass DESIGN_RULES §3 language, §6 workflow, and §10 ship gate.
